|image2 = P.U.C. 5.jpg
|caption2 = A fifth wheel ''(sense 1.1)'' is also a large [[caravan]] or [[travel#Noun|travel]] trailer that is [[connect]]ed to a [[pickup truck]] for [[towing#Noun|towing]] by a hitch similar to the one shown above.
|image3 = The Coach-makers' illustrated hand-book (1875) (14582345340).jpg
|caption3 = A diagram showing the [[gearing#Noun|gearing]] of a [[horse-drawn]] [[coach#Noun|coach]] seen from above.{{refn|group=n|name=n1|From {{cite-book|chapter=Platform Spring Carriage|title=The Coach-makers’ Illustrated Hand-book,{{nb...|[...] Containing Complete Instructions in All the Different Branches of Carriage Building. Adapted to the Wants of Every Person Directly or Indirectly Connected with the Manufacture of Carriages. Written and Revised by Practical Men of Acknowledged Ability and Practical Experience in Their Several Departments.}}|edition=2nd|location=Philadelphia, Pa.|publisher=I[saac] D[elaney] Ware,{{nb...|publisher of The Carriage Monthly.}}|year=1875|section=part II (Blacksmith Department)|page=126|pageurl=https://archive.org/stream/coachmakersillus00ware/coachmakersillus00ware#page/126/mode/1up|oclc=4723107}}.}} The fifth wheel ''(sense 2)'' is the [[circular]] [[component]] in the [[center#Noun|center]] of each [[figure#Noun|figure]].
